WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.832
Welcome to Section Four: Human Resources.

2
00:00:03.032 --> 00:00:05.045
Organizing establishes roles.

3
00:00:05.245 --> 00:00:11.074
Human resources management helps people enter those roles, learn the work, contribute, and develop.

4
00:00:11.274 --> 00:00:17.439
At our fictional Cedar Crossing Library, community workshops now include a new digital registration service.

5
00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:24.092
The manager needs suitable staffing, a clear job description, and a way to prepare employees for the changed work.

6
00:00:24.292 --> 00:00:30.410
We will follow this service from defining a position through selecting, supporting, and reviewing an employee.

7
00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:34.895
The diagram moves through define, select, develop, review, and respond.

8
00:00:35.095 --> 00:00:38.674
Information from each stage can improve earlier decisions.

9
00:00:38.874 --> 00:00:43.595
All Cedar Crossing people, events, and targets are invented teaching examples.

10
00:00:43.795 --> 00:00:46.837
They are separate from the assessed Performance Review Blues case.

11
00:00:47.037 --> 00:00:50.257
This optional lesson supports Chapters Ten through Twelve.

12
00:00:50.457 --> 00:00:54.750
Listen or read, revisit a chapter, and skip or retry any practice.

13
00:00:54.950 --> 00:01:01.398
The goal is to connect management decisions, not to memorize a perfect script for supervising every person.
